   "date": "2019-09-03T16:02:26Z",
   "subject": "Re: Stuck with FALSE command during installation of camtrapR Package",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, <div>R fails to install dependencies of camtrapR (other packages that camtrapR needs to run). Therefore you can&#39;t load camtrapR, even though it installed on your system.</div><div><br></div><div>Try installing the package with:</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">install.packages(&quot;camtrapR&quot;, dependencies = TRUE)</font></div><div><br></div><div>If that fails, try first:</div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">install.packages(&quot;rotl&quot;, dependencies = TRUE)<br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">install.packages(&quot;taxize&quot;, dependencies = TRUE)</font><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Does that help?</font></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Also, when asked this:</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"bookman old style, new york, times, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">  There are binary versions available but the source versions are later:</span></font></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"bookman old style, new york, times, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">       binary source needs_compilation</span></font></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"bookman old style, new york, times, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">rotl    3.0.7  3.0.9             FALSE</span></font></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"bookman old style, new york, times, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">taxize  0.9.6  0.9.8             FALSE</span></font></div></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Does it ask you if you want to install from source? If is asks you, answer no. Install the binary, not source. Installing from source may fail if  there is source code (like C code) in the package which needs to be compiled.</div><div><br></div><div><div>And you may want to consider updating your R. Sometimes that solves problems. See the link for an easy way to update:</div><div><a href=\"https://www.r-statistics.com/2013/03/updating-r-from-r-on-windows-using-the-installr-package/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.r-statistics.com/2013/03/updating-r-from-r-on-windows-using-the-installr-package/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792460711852000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2w3sI7rgf8HL6UJqQRTZk9\">https://www.r-statistics.com/2013/03/updating-r-from-r-on-windows-using-the-installr-package/</a></div></div><div><br></div><div>Any luck with these suggestions?</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
}
